1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,560
Before you try the 30-second chair stand test,

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,380
there is one safety rule you shouldn't ignore.

3
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:09,120
So start the counter, up to 30 seconds.

4
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:11,220
Try to count the number of times that you

5
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:13,580
can stand up on the chair unassisted and then

6
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:14,140
sit down.

7
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:17,780
However, if you feel unsafe, if you got dizziness

8
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:20,280
or ataxia, then don't do this test.

9
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:23,160
Once you have your number, don't compare that to

10
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:25,980
universal number. And even if your score looks

11
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:28,640
low, that number alone doesn't diagnose you.

12
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:31,880
Dr. Rehan explains how to interpret it properly in

13
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:33,040
the full video on the channel.
